  "description": "Subject: Configuration Overview \u2013 Warehouse Sensor Hub (SensorHub\u201101)\n\nThe Warehouse Sensor Hub (device name\u202fSensorHub\u201101) is a gateway\u2011class hub installed on the ceiling of the main warehouse. It aggregates environmental data from temperature, humidity and GPS sensors and forwards the readings to the central monitoring system. The hub\u2019s purpose is described as a ceiling\u2011mounted device that collects ambient conditions and location information for logistics monitoring. It is identified by the gateway ID **5f2a1c3d4b6e7f8a9b0c1d2e**, operates with a system interval of **300\u202fseconds**, and is configured not to retain duplicate measurements. No parent device is assigned to this hub.\n\nThe device is tagged for easy classification: **environment\u202f=\u202fwarehouse** and **department\u202f=\u202flogistics**. Its data model defines two primary attributes:\n\n1. **temperature** \u2013 a numeric reading encoded as `application/json`, representing ambient temperature in Celsius. The attribute carries the tags **unit\u202f=\u202fCelsius** and **sensor\u202f=\u202fthermometer**, and its system aggregation method is set to **MEAN** (with no additional aggregation options or child attributes).\n\n2. **location** \u2013 a GPS\u2011type attribute also using `application/json`, providing the device\u2019s latitude/longitude coordinates. This attribute is tagged **source\u202f=\u202fdevice** and aggregates data using the **LAST** strategy, again without extra options or child attributes."
